{%- comment -%}
  Cellexia Reviews — the app-proxy ROOT path (v1.19, SPEC-1.19 §8).

  Sibling of cx-proxy.liquid, deriving the SAME metafield with the SAME
  fallback and sanitization, but emitting the root instead of the API base:

    cx-proxy  →  "/apps/<subpath>/api"     (JSON endpoints)
    cx-base   →  "/apps/<subpath>"         (this snippet)

  Why a snippet instead of stripping "/api" off cx-proxy's output: string
  surgery on a rendered value depends on a filter being available and on the
  suffix never changing. Deriving both from the same source makes the two
  paths structurally impossible to drift, and a subpath that literally
  contains "api" cannot confuse it.

  Consumers: blocks/reviews-page.liquid builds every crawlable archive link
  ("<base>/reviews?...") from this, and hands the same value to
  assets/cellexia-reviews-page.js as data-proxy (the JS appends "/api/..."
  itself).

  Output contract: exactly "/apps/<subpath>", no surrounding whitespace.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign cx_base_subpath = shop.metafields.cellexia.proxy_path.value | default: '' | append: '' | strip
  assign cx_base_subpath = cx_base_subpath | remove: '/' | remove: ' '
  if cx_base_subpath == blank
    assign cx_base_subpath = 'cellexia-reviews'
  endif
-%}
{{- '/apps/' | append: cx_base_subpath -}}
